From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: glink: make the channel open timeout adjustable

qcom_glink_create_local() waits five seconds for the remote to acknowledge a
channel opened from this side. That is generous for any channel the remote has
already brought up, and it is what every glink user has relied on.

It is not enough when the remote has to create the channel on demand. On a
Motorola Moto G82 5G (SM6375), asking the modem for its diagnostic channels --
DIAG_CNTL, DIAG, DIAG_DATA -- makes it begin a glink channel migration, and the
open never completes within five seconds. Twenty-one seconds after we have
given up and closed the channel out from under it, the modem takes a fatal
error:

	qcom_q6v5_pas 6080000.remoteproc: fatal error received:
	  glink_channel_migration.c:602:Assertion status == GLINK_STATUS_SUCCESS failed
	remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in modem: type fatal error

A channel name the modem has never heard of does not do this: it times out
quietly and the modem carries on. So the migration is real work the modem is
doing on our behalf, and the timeout may well be cutting it off partway.

Make the wait a module parameter so that question can be answered without
rebuilding, and leave the default at the five seconds it has always been. The
parameter is writable at runtime, since the interesting experiment is to raise
it, ask again, and see whether the modem finishes.
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -26,6 +26,25 @@
 #define CREATE_TRACE_POINTS
 #include "qcom_glink_trace.h"
 
+/*
+ * How long qcom_glink_create_local() waits for the remote to acknowledge a
+ * channel we opened. Five seconds is what this driver has always used, and it
+ * is plenty for every channel a Qualcomm modem opens itself. It is not enough
+ * for a channel the modem has to bring up on demand: asking for DIAG_CNTL or
+ * DIAG makes the modem start a channel migration, and the assertion it takes
+ * afterwards
+ *
+ *   glink_channel_migration.c:602: Assertion status == GLINK_STATUS_SUCCESS
+ *
+ * arrives about twenty-one seconds after we have already given up and closed
+ * the channel underneath it. So make the wait adjustable, to find out whether
+ * the modem would have finished if anyone had waited.
+ */
+static unsigned int open_timeout_ms = 5000;
+module_param(open_timeout_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(open_timeout_ms,
+		 "milliseconds to wait for the remote to acknowledge a locally opened channel");
+
 #define GLINK_NAME_SIZE		32
 #define GLINK_VERSION_1		1
 
@@ -1257,11 +1276,13 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto release_channel;
 
-	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&channel->open_ack, 5 * HZ);
+	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&channel->open_ack,
+					  msecs_to_jiffies(open_timeout_ms));
 	if (!ret)
 		goto err_timeout;
 
-	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&channel->open_req, 5 * HZ);
+	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&channel->open_req,
+					  msecs_to_jiffies(open_timeout_ms));
 	if (!ret)
 		goto err_timeout;
 
